{
  "requirement": "An execution error returns `Err` rather than a `Fingerprinted` containing a\ncompleted answer.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation: when execution fails, `verify` returns `Err` and not a `Fingerprinted` holding a completed answer. The parent `validate_node` text says `verify` calls `Criterion::execute` with a fresh context. So the relevant failure classes are an error returned by `execute`, a failure to resolve a node or edge during execution, and a missing agent for an agent-backed criterion.\n\nThe marked tests cover these classes:\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[loading_execution_resolution_and_saving_failures_do_not_publish_answers]` makes `execute` fail and asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"execute\"))`. It reads an unknown node and asserts `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))`. It makes edge resolution fail and asserts `Err(Graph(\"edges\"))`. Each failure returns `Err` and not a value. The test also shows that a load failure does not stop a fresh execution from returning a value, and that a store failure leaves no record.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[resolution_storage_and_callback_errors_are_not_judgments]` has a criterion that reads a missing node inside its callback. `verify` returns `Err(Graph(\"missing\"))`, and no record is written.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[runner_does_not_store_a_missing_agent_error_and_supports_intermediate_calls]` runs an agent-backed criterion with no agent. `verify` returns `Err(NoAgentConfigured)`, and nothing is stored or read. The test then shows a normal `Ok` result once an agent is configured.\n- The other marked tests are `typed_loading_reports_decode_errors_even_for_stale_evidence`, `serialization_failure_leaves_the_existing_record_unchanged` and `malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors`. They cover load, decode and encode error paths and show that successful executions still return values. They add confirmation but are not needed for the core obligation.\n\nA reviewer would find no gap in the failure classes the text names. The assertions use `matches!` on `Err(...)` variants, so a returned `Fingerprinted` would fail them.",
